    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModel">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/ProcessModel"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A model of a data workflow.

An instance of this entity will contain as its substep the beginning pf a sequence of WorkflowModelStep entities, each with a SHACL shape to be applied and (optionally) template key-value pairs.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Workflow model</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelInstance -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelInstance">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModel"/>
        <rdfs:comment>An assignment of entities to the steps of a specific WorkflowModel

A WorkflowModelInstance is composed of one or more WorkflowModelStepAssignment instances that indicate the entities to which the steps are validated against, alongside instructions on how to fetch the next target node(s) of the data workflow.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Workflow model instance</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStep -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStep">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModel"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A WorkflowModelStep entity contains a SHACL shape to be applied to a target node and (optionally) template key-value pairs.

The target nodes will correspond to entities in a data workflow, and are dynamically assigned by the validation process following the WorkflowModelStepAssignment entities related to this step from a WorkflowInstance.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Workflow model step</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStepAssignment -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStepAssignment">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelInstance"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A WorkflowModelStepAssignment instance indicates the entities to which a workflow model step is validated against, alongside a reference to the property with which the validation process will fetch the next target node(s) of the data workflow.

Important: You can find instructions on how to assign workflow model steps to data workflows in the documentation for the assignedEntity property or the Python validation API.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Workflow model step assignment</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStepTemplate -->


    <owl:Class rdf:about="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStepTemplate">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://crc1625.mdi.ruhr-uni-bochum.de/WorkflowModelStep"/>
        <rdfs:comment>A key-&gt;value template with which a WorkflowModelStep will replace values in its assigned SHACL shape.

The key and values are arbitrary strings. The logic for storing/reading/processing these strings must be specified by e.g. extending the WorkflowModel dataclass in Python.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


